    "This hardens existing selected-file-search consumer cancellation, not another native subsystem extraction.",
    "460 is the unique suite size: initial and strict runs execute the same 418 AS and42 client tests; never report920 unique tests.",
    "Three new Preparing tests call SearchRequestProcessor directly with controlled startup/cleanup gates. They do not exercise public JSON-RPC session serialization or native OS-thread cleanup.",
    "At this tested source, public sessionStop is serialized behind pending sessionStart for the same session ID. Reader-intent cancellation and its public acceptance are a separate pending slice.",
    "GUI uses concurrent legacy fuzzyFileSearch with immediate same-token empty-query cancellation; no session protocol migration is implied. New-host real GUI Preparing acceptance is unproved by these library gates.",
    "No fresh installed worker or frozen full CLI/App Server/GUI binary is established by these --lib runs. Actual native/process API gates remain separate evidence.",
    "TUI production and fixtures are outside this AS/client test scope.",
    "Three SDK Python paths were formatted in the same command window; AS/client Rust success does not validate package metadata behavior.",
    "No in-app Browser checks, upstream-updater completion, release or whole-harness completion claim.",
    "Source/archive and generated-test executable preservation is cloud-local; root owns publication identity and external durability."
